  message: "RE-VERIFIED 2026-09-28 at dev 5f80a79081. PREMISE HOLDS; THE PROMISE'S LOCATION IS CORRECTED; THE ROW'S OWN BEHAVIOURAL TEST HAS BEEN RUN. Record: scratchpad lukoz/.\n\nSTILL NO READER: grep of packages/*/src finds trust_level only as the dataclass field (taint.py:222), the YAML parse (taint.py:1563, default 'unknown'), the constructor keyword args, and the AUTO_SINK_ZONE_MAP literals. No read in the propagators or in verify_claims.\n\nWHERE THE PROMISE IS, corrected: it is NOT in 'verify-claims --help' (the rendered help does not mention trust_level). It is in:\n  - cmd_verify_claims's DOCSTRING, cli.py:6254 (was cited as :5985): developer-facing.\n  - docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1511: 'raise trust_level for a sink that is safe in context'. USER-FACING.\n  - docs/hypergumbo-spec.md:1542: 'the supported way for a repo to raise trust_level on a sink that is safe in context'. USER-FACING.\n  So option (b), deprecate, has three sentences to remove, not one.\n\nBEHAVIOURAL TEST, shipped verify-claims (claim host_secret -> subprocess; fixture: os.environ['CMD'] -> subprocess.run in one function):\n  no sink override                                                  violated, 1 flow\n  --taint-sinks: subprocess.run, zone subprocess, trust_level trusted     violated, 1 flow   (identical)\n  --taint-sinks: the same with trust_level untrusted                      violated, 1 flow\n  CONTROL that the override is applied: the same entry with zone vetted_tools -> confirmed_with_caveats, 0 flows. Replacement by (module, name, kind) works. trust_level alone moves nothing."  # 886e
